title": "Genres, narrative conventions, and visual culture"}, {"id": "83be78e6-dea4-4c52-83da-fffb61c2cd58", "type": "concept", "title": "Representation, fandom, and social influence"}], "description": "Students examine audiovisual media as art, industry, ideology, and habit."}, {"id": "fbafb461-e8be-4a78-b0bf-7a3659dbc153", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Streaming and convergence", "children": [{"id": "5b96104d-b70f-4c1e-9d3a-055ff141426e", "type": "concept", "title": "Subscription platforms, recommendation systems, binge viewing, and fragmentation"}, {"id": "41c293ce-7c2d-4a0a-9d8c-8320489b2276", "type": "concept", "title": "Platform competition and global catalogs"}, {"id": "672d834b-4d6e-4c75-971c-60c642b57005", "type": "concept", "title": "Labor, residuals, data, and creative risk"}], "description": "Streaming changes distribution, economics, data, and audience behavior."}]}, {"id": "5237c6a4-7d4f-449c-87b2-633f7cbb6c48", "type": "topic", "title": "Internet, Digital Media, Social Media, and Networked Publics", "description": "Students learn how digital media reshape audiences, participation, identity, attention, and platform power.", "children": [{"id": "9108e50f-d328-4294-86c4-5ebce927fe00", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Networked publics", "children": [{"id": "649326a2-2d86-4e42-834b-e1f199e78869", "type": "concept", "title": "Online identity, context collapse, virality, and participatory culture"}, {"id": "d46140c1-4175-4648-94a9-b9e24bb902e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Creators, influencers, communities, and fandoms"}, {"id": "e3edbc99-b908-49e7-88ef-5eda660d08a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Attention economies and engagement metrics"}], "description": "Students learn how digital environments reshape audience, visibility, and participation."}, {"id": "dac2906b-361a-4236-a5a0-27b75ce05299", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Platform power", "children": [{"id": "1c1ce157-ff9d-421b-b1fa-e4606e631258", "type": "concept", "title": "Algorithms, moderation, recommendation, and ranking"}, {"id": "ea3049db-7aeb-4ae8-8943-a859278ee5a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Data extraction, surveillance, and targeted advertising"}, {"id": "442dea05-e3cf-404d-940e-e7e45ed2201d", "type": "concept", "title": "Platform dependency and deplatforming"}], "description": "Platforms are media infrastructures with rules, incentives, and opaque governance."}, {"id": "38650b82-44d8-4bff-9774-ee89e53425d5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital social change", "children": [{"id": "d10155f7-5677-40d7-91aa-a158207c3568", "type": "concept", "title": "Hashtag activism, civic media, and networked movements"}, {"id": "995ec90b-a6f8-4ad3-9686-96ab338c28c3", "type": "concept", "title": "Harassment, polarization, and amplification"}, {"id": "b1a7b2ab-a753-48af-8bea-63ea952b7d73", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital divides and access inequality"}], "description": "Digital media can mobilize publics and intensify harm."}]}, {"id": "925f802d-af42-4455-ab7c-e7fdd10ef9fe", "type": "topic", "title": "Media Industries, Ownership, Regulation, Policy, and Economics", "description": "This topic analyzes who owns media, how money flows, and how policy shapes public communication.", "children": [{"id": "808e6522-08ce-416d-814c-ee9c808ea850", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ownership and concentration", "children": [{"id": "560fbc9f-7b69-42ea-81a2-241f17d40a25", "type": "concept", "title": "Conglomerates, mergers, chains, private equity, and public media"}, {"id": "9c617bda-5166-4d3c-9cb3-c51746112a33", "type": "concept", "title": "Vertical and horizontal integration"}, {"id": "8c49e2e8-9a3f-4293-bd4b-725f19f498d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Local ownership, diversity, and editorial autonomy"}], "description": "Students learn how ownership structures influence media diversity and independence."}, {"id": "90dec43c-a862-4d37-8395-912779932c90", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Media economics", "children": [{"id": "2f2fef60-ab03-48b9-8a3e-271c116d0aeb", "type": "concept", "