e": "Verification and accountability", "children": [{"id": "6c54d1c0-1c5d-4064-b372-9c9b4d8e1bdc", "type": "concept", "title": "Sourcing, corroboration, fact-checking, and transparency"}, {"id": "a2530add-7dfa-4b71-9d9c-e481d81b8542", "type": "concept", "title": "Corrections, attribution, independence, and conflicts of interest"}, {"id": "6c029692-14af-45c0-b92a-1192376e15c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Investigative reporting and watchdog functions"}], "description": "Journalism's social value depends on disciplined evidence and correction."}, {"id": "58bfbccb-1ac6-477c-930f-aa8c4a5faa5b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Journalism under pressure", "children": [{"id": "e1b5f2f4-3ee3-404c-8a2d-1caf771c977d", "type": "concept", "title": "Economic decline, safety, polarization, political attacks, and public distrust"}, {"id": "a1ee5f5c-6416-4c59-ad85-20a0a2827326", "type": "concept", "title": "Local journalism, nonprofit models, and audience engagement"}, {"id": "ccbc5ac2-d28f-4167-bd8b-18b32db5079e", "type": "concept", "title": "Global press freedom and censorship"}], "description": "Students analyze the pressures facing news organizations."}]}, {"id": "46060b88-bde0-471b-9c37-b3917187060d", "type": "topic", "title": "Advertising, Public Relations, Strategic Communication, and Persuasion Industries", "description": "This module explains how promotional media shape consumption, reputation, advocacy, and public narratives.", "children": [{"id": "40b6966f-3708-4368-87c6-00c740f3d25f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Advertising systems", "children": [{"id": "2436688a-5e87-4cc8-9fc5-04a03a928a7e", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand strategy, creative appeals, media buying, and targeting"}, {"id": "bd5b6c55-ed27-4800-96f3-bf62ad30e568", "type": "concept", "title": "Native advertising, sponsorship, and influencer marketing"}, {"id": "f36c49b5-555a-4ce5-bbeb-5a650384122d", "type": "concept", "title": "Consumer culture and attention capture"}], "description": "Advertising funds much of media and shapes cultural desire."}, {"id": "9fab08fe-411c-48f4-af7f-23134ee6e5ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Public relations and reputation", "children": [{"id": "e41a976c-0bb5-4614-84ff-270921769af2", "type": "concept", "title": "Media relations, stakeholder communication, campaigns, and crisis communication"}, {"id": "19a96657-c52e-4d3a-b52e-b9910012afc6", "type": "concept", "title": "Corporate social responsibility and advocacy"}, {"id": "46d23160-3784-4e92-a5e4-1f4c3646a97a", "type": "concept", "title": "Spin, transparency, and ethical boundaries"}], "description": "PR shapes organizational visibility, trust, and public narratives."}, {"id": "57254f64-cd9b-4643-b58b-958df7cf91f1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Persuasion and society", "children": [{"id": "c3d53631-3a07-45dd-9c69-722f10eb8980", "type": "concept", "title": "Framing, agenda-building, social proof, and emotional appeals"}, {"id": "982eceea-753a-450a-b9bd-6ae9fd5c19ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Political advertising and issue advocacy"}, {"id": "4789890a-7b37-484f-813c-1e7e0e2ad111", "type": "concept", "title": "Regulation, disclosure, and manipulation concerns"}], "description": "Students connect promotional media to power and public influence."}]}, {"id": "05a69d61-6ee0-410f-921f-c4c38a17c0a1", "type": "topic", "title": "Media Effects, Audiences, Reception, Uses, and Everyday Meaning-Making", "description": "Students compare theories of media influence with audience agency, interpretation, and social context.", "children": [{"id": "b70a0d0a-3ba9-494d-b83f-e8a6b0acd1a2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Effects theories", "children": [{"id": "318e7dd0-6520-4fcc-be90-b0d07fc8da97", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultivation, agenda-setting, framing, priming, spiral of silence, and diffusion"}, {"id": "f13e92c3-d5eb-42af-b3e1-9e7fb5bdad3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Moral panic and media violence debates"}, {"id": "b0d50920-d8fa-4afc-bd05-be1a6bc07f80", "type": "concept", "title": "Short-term, long-term, individual, and societal effects"}], "description": "Students compare how scholars explain media influence."}, {"id": "4eaa82f3-e62c-441d-a768-ce00092e38cd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Audience reception", "children": [{"id": "c791477f-2e9b-4fa7-9cf4-510096ee0071", "type": "concept", "title": "Uses and gratifications, encoding/decoding, fandom, and resistance"}, {"id": "0c512149-3cb5-4fba-99f9-55ddc23194b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Interpretive communities and lived experience"}, {"id": "b0a2b0e1-dbbf-44ba-bb12-01c745814ffd", "type": "concept", "title": "Selective exposure and motivated reasoning"}], "description": "Audiences interpret media actively within social contexts."}, {"id": "58c4754b-c40f-4f6c-bd86-3499451a2a34", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Everyday media life", "children": [{"id": "3f9dfdc7-5f31-4a96-90ed-1e08e5429347", "type": "concept", "title": "Media routines, multitasking, parasocial relationships, and emotional regulation"}, {"id": "827c184e-f4f7-4026-b87a-136eb0f0bdeb", "type": "concept", "title": "Family, peer, and workplace media practices"}, {"id": "129e7bb4-4684-423f-81e3-3c692181ae08", "type": "concept", "title": "Media diaries and reflective analysis"}], "description": "The course connects theory to daily habits and identity."}]}, {"id": "0e776489-9bfe-4dab-b829-70e58942f2c2", "type": "topic", "title": "Representation, Identity, Race, Gender, Class, Disability, and Culture", "description": "This topic centers how media represent groups, normalize power, and enable counter-narratives.", "children": [{"id": "a50fdcae-42eb-4f5c-bd66-0ebb9031290d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Representation and power", "children": [{"id": "e51985aa-31e6-442e-8f12-dc50356d467d", "type": "concept", "title": "Stereotypes, visibility, erasure, and normalization"}, {"id": "faee0e85-1b34-4b9b-b222-4fe4dba6a6a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Race, gender, class, disability, sexuality, age, and religion"}, {"id": "2d376156-5e0b-4b03-8153-e25420cfd4fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Framing, casting, authorship, and voice"}], "description": "Students learn how media images shape social knowledge."}, {"id": "90fd0ecd-2b7b-4b64-98a7-2be361ecf910", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cultural studies", "children": [{"id": "85e6ef35-1f39-4b23-8083-72bba91abf1b", "type": "concept", "title": "Ideology, hegemony, semiotics, and popular culture"}, {"id": "16e98dbc-e529-49bc-940f-1e3af436c80c", "type": "concept", "title": "Counterpublics and alternative media"}, {"id": "f88f3f06-e999-44cb-9ac5-4cd1faed2ab7", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural critique and audience agency"}], "description": "Media are sites where power, pleasure, and resistance meet."}, {"id": "71f8278d-0f3e-4895-a81b-a1cf4f77a42f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inclusive media practice", "children": [{"id": "39e14e1b-5463-42d6-a9f5-de09cf97c329", "type": "concept", "title": "Source diversity, visual ethics, and language choices"}, {"id": "849e9cec-3982-4d26-8326-6041e8fe6be8", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessibility, captions, alt text, and inclusive design"}, {"id": "72cc3376-c90a-45ae-876d-354e333d8dea", "type": "concept", "title": "Community review and accountability"}], "description": "Students evaluate how media can represent people with dignity and accuracy."}]}, {"id": "7cf46619-36f8-417a-bffa-06bf57f8b8c2", "type": "topic", "title": "Global Media, Cultural Flows, Localization, and Transnational Communication", "description": "Students explore global media circulation, cultural hybridity, media imperialism, and local adaptation.", "children": [{"id": "9405645d-f579-4fd0-9124-7fa3051b1a75", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global media systems", "children": [{"id": "dac08c02-f1ae-4290-9c23-8bb6421a553b", "type": "concept", "title": "Global news, entertainment formats, streaming, sports, music, and gaming"}, {"id": "05205e43-4b55-47b7-ba55-964bcd2ab564", "type": "concept", "title": "Media imperialism, dependency, and soft power"}, {"id": "eb497567-f544-4481-8686-5da727a3fb9c", "type": "concept", "title": "Public diplomacy and global communication"}], "description": "Students examine how media industries and texts move across borders."}, {"id": "c891a1d7-c855-4104-9d22-4812be7ccea5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Localization and hybridity", "children": [{"id": "4524727e-9bcb-4d5b-ab2a-d1afbcdb4653", "type": "concept", "title": "Glocalization, transcreation, dubbing, subtitling, and format adaptation"}, {"id": "ad08ade8-c8e0-4633-8f95-f59f012a7971", "type": "concept", "title": "Diaspora media and transnational publics"}, {"id": "535f5039-263d-4556-b524-3de65069a281", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural hybridity and authenticity debates"}], "description": "Global media are adapted, remixed, and contested locally."}, {"id": "85b46eeb-24bc-4bbc-b74b-bccb597362d5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global inequality", "children": [{"id": "3eac3838-18e3-4c76-a7c8-a3ce7f7ad9af", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital divides, censorship, platform access, and surveillance"}, {"id": "9dbcfcc1-9aa3-46ef-bea1-7e75298b597b", "type": "concept", "title": "Global South media and alternative publics"}, {"id": "2015adca-85d4-4f3b-9642-9880e239a013", "type": "concept", "title": "Journalist safety and press freedom"}], "description": "Media flows are shaped by unequal infrastructure, capital, and regulation."}]}, {"id": "cf4d265b-f481-4e50-85da-5627933e0d79", "type": "topic", "title": "Misinformation, Disinformation, Media Literacy, and Trust", "description": "This module teaches students to evaluate information credibility, platform dynamics, and public trust in media.", "children": [{"id": "08614751-0b71-451f-8da1-3d3124f182e6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Information disorder", "children": [{"id": "6f427582-e214-47b9-99f8-b66605477fc6", "type": "concept", "title": "False context, manipulated media, impostor content, and conspiracy narratives"}, {"id": "be14dd7e-2cb1-470b-9463-29666e8957c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Bot networks, coordinated influence, and platform incentives"}, {"id": "8fb244d9-33b7-49af-9721-ee41fc9f6154", "type": "concept", "title": "Health, election, climate, and crisis misinformation"}], "description": "Students learn to distinguish misinformation, disinformation, malinformation, rumor, and propaganda."}, {"id": "a428da8d-a230-4fae-b376-2aec79f1b161", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Media literacy", "children": [{"id": "3aabea8e-aa5c-4282-89e5-fdb1a200e2e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Lateral reading, source tracing, verification, and fact-checking"}, {"id": "b2fa4fca-dd3d-49f8-8733-eddf3975a4a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual verification and reverse image search"}, {"id": "509a29b0-10b4-4536-823c-d5940c13eb77", "type": "concept", "title": "Algorithm awareness and emotional manipulation"}], "description": "The point is to build habits for evaluating credibility and evidence."}, {"id": "f4b21401-3992-4d65-8663-09817931f670", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trust and repair", "children": [{"id": "1433abc1-bcdd-43ce-bb3b-83a254a4cd3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparency, corrections, community engagement, and explanatory journalism"}, {"id": "329122df-8f0d-4081-a419-35ba143c2fac", "type": "concept", "title": "Polarization, identity, and selective distrust"}, {"id": "4794a783-61e4-4066-a596-af83c2953896", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional accountability and audience relationships"}], "description": "Students analyze why trust in media changes and how it can be rebuilt."}]}, {"id": "9691a935-2910-4cb7-a1d6-c90075644d68", "type": "topic", "title": "Media Law, Ethics, Privacy, Copyright, Free Speech, and Platform Governance", "description": "Students learn the legal and ethical frameworks that shape media practice and public accountability.", "children": [{"id": "24125933-7940-4119-800b-a472e7591fbb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Media law basics", "children": [{"id": "89328488-35e7-4cf5-9387-1d589de24b31", "type": "concept", "title": "Fir